text: >-
  < Official Judicial V...

  Announcement of

  JUDICIAL VACANCY

  January 17, 2025

  Applications are now being accepted for the position of district court judge
  in the Fourth District Court.

  (Counties include Juab, Millard, Utah and Wasatch).

  This position results from the retirement of Judge Robert C. Lunnen, August 1,
  2025.

  Applications must be submitted online by Tuesday, Feb

  uary 18, 2025.

  Application Forms and Instructions

  To apply go to judicialvacancy.utah.gov and complete the online judicial 325

  contact Monica Taylor at 801-538-1856 or monicataylor@utah.gov.

  stions, please

  Selection Process

  of district court judge in the Fourth Dis

  Utah law requires the Judicial Nominating Commission to s

  Allard, Utah and Wasatch).

  meeting. The Governor has 30 days in which to make a sel

  reject the governor's selection. To obtain the procedures o

  of Judge Robert C. Lunnen, August 1, 2025.

  members call 801) 538-1856.

  At its first meeting the Nominating Commission accepts p

  nline by Tuesday, February 18, 2025.

  Terms o.

  A. Benefits

  ial application form. If you hay

  Minimum Requirements: Under Article VIII, Section 7 of the Utah

  e at least 30

  years old, and judges of other courts of records must be at least 25 years ola

  Residency: All justices and judges must be United State citizens. Supreme
  Court Jus

  an residents for at least

  five years immediately preceding selection. Judges of other courts of record
  must be residents of Utah for at least three years

  preceding selection.

  Practice of Law: All justices and judges must be admitted to practice law in
  Utah, but need not actually engage in the practice

  Retirement Program: Judges are able to retire at any age with 25 years
  service; at age 62 with 10 years service; or at age 70

  with 6 years service. Retirement amount is calculated on the basis of years of
  service and an average of the last 2 years of salary.

  Judges receive 5% of their final average salary for each of their first 10
  years of service, 2.25% of their average salary for each

  year from 11 to 20 years of service, and 1% of their final average salary for
  each year beyond 20 years.

  The annual salary is $213,900 for a District Court Judge • 20 days paid
  vacation per year • 11 paid holidays • $25,000 term life

  insurance policy (with an option to purchase $300,000 more at group rates) •
  Choice of medical and dental plans. All plans

  require a small employee contribution.
